From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taynotfound <marztayron@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rain-1030: power off straight after the disk sync

U1 (1029): slide to power off froze right after "syncing disks...
Killing all processes"; T1 got as far as the root unmount. The SoC
wedges at a varying step once the kernel kills what is left. launchd
has torn userspace down already: sync, wait for busy buffers, then
PEHaltRestart, before IOKit's process-exit notification.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c b/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
index 8281025..34dc6a5 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_shutdown.c
@@ -224,6 +224,24 @@ reboot_kernel(int howto, char *message)
 
 	lck_mtx_unlock(&vm_swap_data_lock);
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * rain: past this point slide to power off wedged the whole SoC at a different step each time
+	 * (killing processes, the root unmount): the screen stayed on, USB and timers stopped. launchd has
+	 * torn userspace down already, so write the disks and go straight to the PMIC/PSCI path.
+	 */
+	if ((howto & RB_PANIC) == 0) {
+		int busy = 0;
+		if ((howto & RB_NOSYNC) == 0) {
+			sync((proc_t)NULL, (void *)NULL, (int *)NULL);
+			for (int i = 0; i < 50 && (busy = count_busy_buffers()) != 0; i++) {
+				delay_for_interval(100, 1000 * 1000);
+			}
+		}
+		printf("RAIN: disks synced (%d busy), %s now\n", busy, (howto & RB_HALT) ? "power off" : "restart");
+		PEHaltRestart((howto & RB_HALT) ? kPEHaltCPU : kPERestartCPU);
+	}
+#endif
 	/*
 	 * Notify the power management root domain that the system will shut down.
 	 */
